From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: matisse3g: configure SD card detect pin

Describe GPIO38 pin configuration explicitly rather than inheriting the
bootloader's pull-up. Samsung's SM-T531 gpiomux table configures this card
detect input as GPIO, 2 mA, with no pull in both active and sleep states.
Keep the existing active-low card detection wiring.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
@@ -117,3 +117,12 @@
 &pm8226_l21 {
 	regulator-allow-set-load;
 };
+
+&sdhc2_default_state {
+	card-detect-pins {
+		pins = "gpio38";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+};
-- 
